    "body": "Two pronunciation lessons from the Beam blog explainer video (2026-10-17).\n\n- **AIME** — `pronunciation.json` lexicon `AIME → Aime`. `pron_check` heard the written AIME as \"M\" in every carrier. `Aime` (read \"aim\", the usual reading) comes back as AIM in a short sentence. In a long line Whisper still writes M, so the evidence row says to treat that as an ASR artifact.\n- **scatter** — Whisper heard it as \"Statter\" and no respelling passed. It goes in the reword table: the narration says 「先 gather，算完再分发回去」 and the term stays on screen.\n\nChecks: `pron_check --script` reports 0 issues after the change, and the rendered video went through QA.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
